   -> check sign-in #8: example http://127.0.0.1:50000/callback nonce=c82fb56107fe74a0d3679f844d9b0a20
@61000 sign-in #8 checked: https://id.example bob
   -> store #9: identity login example https://id.example bob
@61000 store answers #9: login ok, account 2 None
   -> event: conn#9: account 2 signed in with example
   -> send conn#9 SignedIn example:bob 200b… (32 bytes)
@61000 conn#9 closed: the client left
   -> event: conn#9: closed: the client left
@61000 conn#10 accepted on game from 10.0.0.1
   -> event: conn#10: accepted on game
@61000 conn#10 sends Hello protocol=4 "openm2 test"
   -> event: conn#10: openm2 test speaks protocol 4
   -> send conn#10 Welcome protocol=4
@61000 conn#10 sends TicketLogin example:bob 200b… (32 bytes)
   -> event: conn#10: account 2 joined the game server
   -> store #10: load characters of 2
@61000 store answers #10: characters []
   -> send conn#10 Empire 0
   -> send conn#10 Phase 1
   -> send conn#10 CharacterList []
@61000 conn#11 accepted on auth from 10.0.0.1
   -> event: conn#11: accepted on auth
@61000 conn#11 sends Hello protocol=4 "openm2 test"
   -> event: conn#11: openm2 test speaks protocol 4
   -> send conn#11 Welcome protocol=4
@61000 conn#11 sends StartSignIn
   -> send conn#11 SignInOptions [example] nonce="502a43c73518705f3d6e16ba5399778f"
@61000 conn#11 sends ProviderLogin example http://127.0.0.1:50000/callback
   -> check sign-in #11: example http://127.0.0.1:50000/callback nonce=502a43c73518705f3d6e16ba5399778f
@61000 sign-in #11 checked: https://id.example bob
   -> store #12: identity login example https://id.example bob
@61000 store answers #12: login ok, account 2 None
   -> event: conn#11: login refused: the account is in game
   -> send conn#11 LoginRefused 2
   -> close conn#11
   -> event: conn#11: closed: the account is in game
